  "id": "land-cover-2017",
  "title": "NYC Land Cover 2017 (6-inch, 8 classes)",
  "description": "A 6-inch resolution, 8-class land cover map of New York City, derived from the 2017 LiDAR capture and 2016 orthoimagery. Each pixel holds one class: tree canopy, grass/shrubs, bare soil, water, buildings, roads, other impervious, or railroads. The map was made for the city's Urban Tree Canopy assessment, so it maps from the top down: canopy that hangs over a road or a building counts as tree canopy. This is a mirror of the [NYC Open Data release](https://data.cityofnewyork.us/d/he6d-2qns), converted without changes to pixel values to a Cloud Optimized GeoTIFF in New York State Plane Long Island feet (EPSG:2263). The [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) shows how to read pixels and compute class areas without downloading the file.",
  "license": "other",
